WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.932
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book two.

2
00:00:05.232 --> 00:00:08.595
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.895 --> 00:00:14.555
Unit nineteen: Local Events. Today you will talk about future plans with the present continuous.

4
00:00:14.855 --> 00:00:17.345
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.417
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.283 --> 00:00:23.424
Local event.

7
00:00:24.417 --> 00:00:27.577
Local event means an activity that happens in your area.

8
00:00:28.183 --> 00:00:30.717
There's a local event at the park on Sunday.

9
00:00:31.317 --> 00:00:34.248
Your turn. Say: Local event.

10
00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.275
Local event.

11
00:00:39.017 --> 00:00:39.995
Festival.

12
00:00:40.983 --> 00:00:43.726
Festival means a special time of celebration.

13
00:00:44.317 --> 00:00:46.374
The rice festival is next month.

14
00:00:46.983 --> 00:00:49.752
Your turn. Say: Festival.

15
00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:53.485
Festival.

16
00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:55.309
Attend.

17
00:00:56.317 --> 00:00:58.339
Attend means to go to an event.

18
00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:01.066
Many families attend the concert.

19
00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:04.453
Your turn. Say: Attend.

20
00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.336
Attend.

21
00:01:09.083 --> 00:01:10.305
Community center.

22
00:01:11.317 --> 00:01:14.477
Community center means a building where local people meet.

23
00:01:15.083 --> 00:01:17.652
The dance class is at the community center.

24
00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:21.309
Your turn. Say: Community center.

25
00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:25.435
Community center.

26
00:01:26.183 --> 00:01:27.486
Celebration.

27
00:01:28.483 --> 00:01:31.435
Celebration means a happy event for a special day.

28
00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:34.108
The celebration lasted all night.

29
00:01:34.717 --> 00:01:37.590
Your turn. Say: Celebration.

30
00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:41.632
Celebration.

31
00:01:42.383 --> 00:01:43.605
Organize.

32
00:01:44.617 --> 00:01:47.382
Organize means to plan and arrange an event.

33
00:01:47.983 --> 00:01:50.053
Students organize the school fair.

34
00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:53.395
Your turn. Say: Organize.

35
00:01:56.233 --> 00:01:57.258
Organize.

36
00:01:58.017 --> 00:01:59.169
Participate.

37
00:02:00.183 --> 00:02:02.926
Participate means to take part in an activity.

38
00:02:03.517 --> 00:02:05.992
Everyone can participate in the race.

39
00:02:06.583 --> 00:02:09.305
Your turn. Say: Participate.

40
00:02:12.167 --> 00:02:13.365
Participate.

41
00:02:14.117 --> 00:02:14.955
Tradition.

42
00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:19.111
Tradition means a custom passed down over many years.

43
00:02:19.717 --> 00:02:21.914
Flying kites is a local tradition.

44
00:02:22.517 --> 00:02:24.995
Your turn. Say: Tradition.

45
00:02:27.833 --> 00:02:28.695
Tradition.

46
00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:33.023
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:33.883 --> 00:02:35.894
Visal, what are you doing this weekend?

48
00:02:36.983 --> 00:02:40.167
We're attending the kite festival at the community center!

49
00:02:41.283 --> 00:02:42.760
Are you participating?

50
00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:48.174
Yes! My father and I are flying a big kite on Saturday.

51
00:02:49.283 --> 00:02:50.760
Who is organizing it?

52
00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:55.640
The village leaders are organizing it. It's an old tradition.

53
00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:58.521
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:59.383 --> 00:03:03.310
Grammar focus: Present continuous for future plans.

55
00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:04.832
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:05.517 --> 00:03:07.586
We are attending the festival this weekend.

57
00:03:08.483 --> 00:03:10.506
I'm meeting my friends on Saturday.

58
00:03:11.417 --> 00:03:12.847
Are you coming tomorrow?

59
00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:17.994
Use the present continuous with a future time for plans you have already arranged.

60
00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:22.552
Be careful! Don't say: We attending the festival this weekend.

61
00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:27.835
Say: We are attending the festival this weekend.

62
00:03:28.135 --> 00:03:31.005
Don't forget am, is or are before the -ing verb.

63
00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:34.371
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:36.737
A Busy Weekend in Town.

65
00:03:37.037 --> 00:03:40.104
Our town organizes many local events throughout the year.

66
00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:44.330
There are festivals, concerts and celebrations for everyone.

67
00:03:45.333 --> 00:03:49.237
This weekend, we are attending a kite festival at the community center.

68
00:03:50.233 --> 00:03:53.928
On Sunday, my class is participating in a traditional dance.

69
00:03:54.933 --> 00:03:58.640
I love these events because they keep our local traditions alive.

70
00:03:59.733 --> 00:04:04.141
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:04.983 --> 00:04:07.412
We blank attending the festival on Sunday.

72
00:04:07.712 --> 00:04:10.878
A, are. B, is. C, will.

73
00:04:14.433 --> 00:04:16.549
The answer is A: are.

74
00:04:17.683 --> 00:04:20.031
To take part in an activity is to blank.

75
00:04:20.331 --> 00:04:23.950
A, participate. B, attend. C, organize.

76
00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.894
The answer is A: participate.

77
00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:33.595
A building where local people meet is a blank.

78
00:04:33.895 --> 00:04:38.083
A, community center. B, festival. C, tradition.

79
00:04:41.633 --> 00:04:44.016
The answer is A: community center.

80
00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:48.026
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:48.883 --> 00:04:51.150
What is a local event you enjoy attending?

82
00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:01.474
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:05:01.774 --> 00:05:10.254
I enjoy the boat races near my house. Next month, my family is attending the races, and my uncle is rowing in one of the boats!

84
00:05:10.554 --> 00:05:12.159
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:18.059
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and present continuous for future plans.

86
00:05:18.359 --> 00:05:22.846
Today's value is community spirit. Help and care for people in your town.

87
00:05:23.146 --> 00:05:25.845
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

88
00:05:26.145 --> 00:05:28.646
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

